ATTRIBUTION

This is an independent implementation, not a fork. No source code from the
projects below has been copied into it.

  YAMN -- Yet Another Mix Net
  Copyright (C) Steve Crook
  https://github.com/crooks/yamn
  MIT licence

  nymserv -- GnuPG-based pseudonymous email server ("Zax-style")
  Copyright (C) 2012 Steve Crook
  https://github.com/crooks/nymserv
  GPL

nymserv-ng interoperates with the YAMN network and follows the Zax-style
nymserver model. It reuses the Config: header grammar, the reserved-name
conventions and the alias-expiry concept from nymserv as an interface
contract, so that existing clients remain usable. The implementation, the
architecture, the cryptography and the delivery model are new.

The mix network concept originates with:

  D. Chaum, "Untraceable Electronic Mail, Return Addresses, and Digital
  Pseudonyms", Communications of the ACM, 24(2), 1981.

The earliest pseudonym server, penet.fi, was operated by Johan Helsingius
until 1996. Its closure under legal pressure is the reason section 4.4 of the
design document exists.
